### Also check Ansible's temporary directories

Local modules are copied into temporary directories before execution. If `/tmp`, `~/.ansible/tmp`, permissions, filesystem, or mount behavior is bad, Ansible can appear to freeze.

Run:

```bash
ls -ld /tmp
ls -ld ~/.ansible
ls -ld ~/.ansible/tmp 2>/dev/null || true
df -h /tmp "$HOME"
df -i /tmp "$HOME"
```

`/tmp` should normally look like:

```text
drwxrwxrwt
```

The final `t` is important.

Test it:

```bash
touch /tmp/test-$USER
rm -f /tmp/test-$USER
```

And:

```bash
mkdir -p ~/.ansible/tmp
chmod 700 ~/.ansible/tmp
touch ~/.ansible/tmp/test
rm ~/.ansible/tmp/test
```

