### I would make localhost explicit in the inventory

Your `hosts.ini` should preferably include a dedicated local group. For example:

```ini
[masters]
master01 ansible_host=10.174.161.22
master02 ansible_host=10.174.161.23
master03 ansible_host=10.174.161.24

[workers]
# workers here

[local]
localhost ansible_connection=local ansible_become=false
```

However, because `group_vars/all.yml` still applies to every inventory host, an even cleaner approach is to create:

```text
inventory/dev/host_vars/localhost.yml
```

with:

```yaml
---
ansible_connection: local
ansible_become: false
ansible_python_interpreter: "{{ ansible_playbook_python }}"
```

That explicitly overrides your global cluster settings for localhost.

Your structure becomes:

```text
inventory/dev/
├── hosts.ini
├── group_vars/
│   └── all.yml
└── host_vars/
    └── localhost.yml
```

I strongly recommend that setup.

